                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="587-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Audix F10</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>Part of Audix&#8217; Fusion series, the F10 &#8220;dynamic instrument microphone&#8221; is a compact, low-cost dynamic intended for use on percussion, drums, and guitar cabinet. </p><p>The &#8220;tailored&#8221; frequency response shows aggressive peaks (+5dB) at 80-90 Hz and 4000-5000 Hz.</p><p>The body is zinc alloy, finished in black. The mic is supplied in a soft pouch and carries a five-year warranty.</p><p>The body has an integrated mic clip, but is compatible with the company&#8217;s DFLEX rim clamp (from the D1, D2, D4 series) as well as the DCLAMP (tension-rod mount) and DVICE (spring-loaded rim clamp), all available separately.</p><p>See also Audix&#8217; D-series microphones, which are functionally similar to the Fusion drum mics. The D2 and D4 have a &#8220;Very Low Mass&#8221; diaphragm that makes them quicker (better transient response) and more accurate. Also, the D series mics are hypercardioid, which might offer superior isolation.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audix/F10">Audix F10</a> is also known as: F-10.</p>
